{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAQ2mbxi3kF9Sbg6Mat5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added `watch::Receiver::mark_unchanged()` to `tokio/src/sync/watch.rs`. It's the opposite of `mark_changed()`: it sets the receiver's seen version to the channel's current version without borrowing the value. After calling it, `has_changed()` returns `false` and `changed()` waits for the next send. It doesn't touch the closed state, so `has_changed()` still returns `Err` once the sender has been dropped.\n\nI also added a `rx_mark_unchanged` test in `tokio/tests/sync_watch.rs`. It covers clearing a change after `mark_changed()` and after a real `send`.\n\nGATE PASS: the test fails without the change (because the method doesn't exist yet) and passes with it. Both `rx_mark*` tests pass. The first gate run failed only because `cargo -p tokio` is ambiguous in this workspace, so I reran it with `--manifest-path tokio/Cargo.toml`.\n\nI only ran the `sync_watch` tests matching `rx_mark`, not the full test suite, doc tests or loom."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":564,"cache_read_input_tokens":34006,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":564,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":357,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0b8778c2-8087-4a0b-9760-7d94044ad012","uuid":"255a0a67-7da4-4c77-b5fe-11301b0ea75e","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:17:19.201Z","request_id":"req_011CgAQ2mPZDVC4wm2ofxcJp"}
